From 7355239b48957b9533c1e9586eeeeadbe2e83d8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:25:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(harbor_agent): chisel and OpenCode from binaries the
 sandbox platform mounts

The sandbox platform can mount the agent binaries into every pod (on Breithorn: read-only image
volumes under /opt/rl-tools/<name>/<version>/). Then nothing has to be uploaded per sandbox:

- model_tunnel.pod_install: mounted uses chisel at pod_binary as it is. No upload, no chmod (the
  mount is read-only), the server log goes to /tmp/.nemo-gym-chisel.log (pod_log), and the start
  fails unless the binary prints chisel_version. chisel_dir then needs only the node's binary.
- opencode_install: mounted with opencode_bin: setup runs a check script instead of an install
  (executable, `--version` = version; otherwise agent setup fails, failure class infra as for a
  failed install), and the run calls the binary by that path.

installed_compat.check_mounted_binary holds the check for any adapter. upload stays the default
for both.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
